ts trying to cover  what you've now suppressed  yeah all of the major papers may have an  environmental journalist  and so there may be the occasional  article that david attenborough but if  you look at the rest of the sum  they run a campaign to promote fracking  across britain they've staged  false fracking protests they have run a  campaign to cut taxes on fossil fuels  for 10 years  that has taken 110 billion pounds out of  the nhs and the  the government coffers that could have  been invested in a green new deal  and so therefore the overwhelming  coverage in in the murdoch's paper  and the billionaire press is  anti-climate action anti-investment in a  green new deal  across the world murdoch is is  recognized as an impediment to climate  action  his own son james has quit news core  over the issue  and so what we are saying today is we  want those five tax haven billionaires  to ensure their corporations take this  seriously and help protect britain  do you support i mean you clearly do  support the method of doing so but you  seem to have managed to unite  very different parts of the political  spectrum against what you've done today  i mean obviously the home secretary  pretty patel has criticized what you've  done  the labor um shadow minister  for the in culture media and sport has  said a free press is vital for our  democracy  people have the right to read what they  want stopping them from being  distributed and printers from doing  their jobs is wrong  even the leader one of the leaders of  reporters without borders the  international ngo  for press freedom has said there is this  is a clear danger in reducing media  plurality  and restricting access to information i  mean you're managing to  to to garner a lot of criticism from  people whose support you need  well the idea that britain has a diverse  press is a joke  over 70 to 80 percent of our media is  owned by five people  who are they they live offshore in tax  havens how  the idea that britain has a diverse  media is farcical  or every single election for the last 45  years  has been the prime minister has been  backed by rupert murdoch  but what do you think is reduced he's  reduced that diversity  what you've done today is reduced that  diversity even further in terms of the  choice people have today on their  newsstand  that's absolutely untrue what we were  actually saying for the last 45 years  murdoch and rothermere and the barclay  brothers have been heard  over above everybody else in this  country it is time for just one day  that those of us who passionately  believe that britain is under threat  of extreme danger according to un should  be heard and that's why we've come today  because that complacency  by those five men is a threat to bret  threat to britain  however they still print um extinction  rebellions own views  gail bradbook one of your co-founders  only 24 hours ago had a piece in the  evening standard  one of the action one of the targets of  your action  the the idea that you have one article  from gail bradford an interview and then  20 pages on  cruises flights meat eating um  consumption consumerism  our entire press creates the com the  permission for a high carbon lifestyle  and doesn't move us towards where we  need to be what we are here today is  saying is  the media is acting as chamberlain at  the delaying action to 2050  and what we need is a churchillian  action to death britain and the natural  world we've lost 83 percent of nature  and the government has announced  planning system that will destroy more  of nature  we by the time i die we may have lost  all of nature that was on the planet  when i was born this is the christ and  that's why we're here today  donald mccarthy uh thank you very much  indeed for your time appreciate it today  i'll speak to you again  i imagine very soon because there's 10  days of protests  from extinction rebellion that are  taking place at the moment that as uh  you will have seen coverage of on sky  news

